
  .headwater/taxonomy.lock is a derived artifact, and this merge did not reconcile it.

  It holds a fold over the whole corpus, and both sides moved it. A merge of the two
  would state a value true of neither tree. The current side deleted it, and the path is
  marked conflicted.

  Finish the merge, then rebuild it and stage it. Where the lock is conflicted too,
  resolve it first, because every generated file records the lock:

      headwater taxonomy resolve
      git add .headwater/taxonomy.lock

  `headwater taxonomy resolve --check` holds the result.

